# 17. SECURITY RULES

Create real Firestore and Cloud Storage Security Rules in the project.

They must enforce:

- Public reads only for permitted published-resource metadata.
- Public file access only for approved published resources, according to the chosen Storage access design.
- Authentication for uploads.
- Ownership restrictions for pending submissions.
- No ordinary-user modification or deletion of published resource records.
- No ordinary-user overwrite or deletion of existing uploaded files.
- Admin-only moderation.
- Validated fields and allowed status transitions.
- Protection for private user data and moderation records.

A client-side role check is not sufficient.

If some checks require trusted server logic, implement that logic or document precisely what remains to be configured. Never claim that an incomplete rule set guarantees security.

Ensure the chosen Storage design supports the desired public preview and download experience without exposing unpublished files.

